{
  "dom_id": "step-q12488",
  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "Find the coefficient of ${s}^{5}$ in the expansion of  $(3+2s)^{5}.$",
  "worked_solution": "Since the exponent of the binomial expression is $n=5,$ we see that the exponents of the binomial expansion must follow the pattern\n\n$$\n{s}^{0},\\,{s}^{1},\\,{s}^{2},\\,{s}^{3},\\,{s}^{4},\\,{s}^{5}.\n$$\n\nOf these, the term that returns ${s}^{5}$ is the fifth. So, we are looking for the fifth term in the binomial expansion.\n\nThe $5$th row in Pascal's Triangle is $(1,5,10,10,5,1).$ Therefore, the fifth term in the binomial expansion is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1(3)^{0}(2s)^{5} & =32{s}^{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the coefficient of ${s}^{5}$ in the expansion of $(3+2s)^{5}$ is $32.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
